## Error envelope size versus JSON escaping

`simulatorapi.MinResponseBytes` (2048) is documented as always holding a
complete error envelope with a clamped message, a run ID and a field path.
The clamp counts bytes before JSON escaping, so text made of characters that
escape to six bytes (`<`, `>`, `&`, control bytes) can produce an envelope of
about 7 KB; `simulatorapi/capacity_test.go` records that bound as
`errorEnvelopeBytes`. The shipped budgets are far above it, so this only
affects a custom configuration at the documented minimum. Decide whether to
clamp after escaping or raise the documented minimum.
